>> title: Chili con Carne, Instant Pot
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, chiles, texas, one-pot, stew, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> dish: chili-con-carne
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> aka: chili, bowl of red, Texas red, chili no beans, instant pot chili, pressure cooker chili con carne
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 35 min
>> slack: narrow — the ground chile scorches against a sealed base and the lid means nobody sees it happen until it is bitter
>> washing-up: the Instant Pot
>> keeps: 4 days — better on the second; the sealed pot cannot reduce, so it is thinner cold than the stovetop one

Bloom the chile with the pot switched off. Pour the tomatoes over the top and do not stir them down.

>> step: brown 12 min, in two batches
Brown @beef chuck{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 1/2-in dice), @kosher salt{2%tsp} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} on sauté in an #Instant Pot{} for ~brown{12%min}, in two batches.

>> step: soften
Soften @yellow onion{1%large}(chopped), @garlic{6%cloves}(minced) with @&(~1)browned beef{}.

>> step: bloom the chile off the heat
Bloom @ancho chile powder{1/4%cup}(30 g; pure ground chile, not a chili-powder blend), @ground cumin{1%Tbs}, @dried oregano{1%tsp} in @&(~1)pot{} with the heat switched off, then scrape the base until nothing is stuck to it.

>> step: 35 min high pressure, natural release 15 min
Pressure cook @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{2%cup}(475 mL), @crushed tomatoes{14%oz}(400 g; poured over, not stirred down), @cider vinegar{1%Tbs}, lid on and valve sealed: ~come to pressure{12%min}, then ~pressure cook{35%min} on high and ~natural release{15%min}.

>> step: thicken with masa, lid off
Thicken @&(~1)chili{} with @masa harina{2%Tbs}(20 g; slaked in a little water) on sauté for ~thicken{8%min}, lid off.
